{#-
  PASS 1 — user prompt, one render per paper.

  Available here:
    paper.title, paper.text, paper.paper_id, paper.strategy, paper.words
    project, min_subtopics, max_subtopics
    extra_fields  — the [{name, type, description}] declared in config.yaml

  The field list below must stay in step with the response schema: the six core
  fields are fixed in code, and anything you add belongs in topics.extra_fields
  so that the schema and this prompt grow together.
-#}
Read this paper and describe what it is about.

{{ paper.text }}

---

Report:

- main_topic: the single research area this paper belongs to, 2-5 words.
- subtopics: {{ min_subtopics }}-{{ max_subtopics }} more specific themes, each
  1-4 words. Include the problem addressed, the method family used, and any
  distinctive resource, material or phenomenon studied.
- task: the problem the paper addresses, or "n/a" if it is a resource, survey or
  position paper.
- method_family: the dominant technical approach, named the way your field names
  it rather than described in a sentence.
- contribution_type: one of "resource", "model", "evaluation", "analysis",
  "application", "position", "survey".
- one_line_summary: a single sentence, at most 25 words, that could be read
  aloud when introducing the paper.
{% for field in extra_fields %}
- {{ field.name }}: {{ field.description or "as described in config.yaml" }}
{%- if field.type == "list[str]" %} Give a list.{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
